          <msContents>
            <summary>Collection of short tracts on urines, pulse, regimen, etc.: in Latin. Followed by medical receipts in German. By Several hands. 

The Latin portion of the MS. ends at fol. 64, and seems to be by the same hand eith headings and paragraph marks in red. The remainder contains the receipts, by several hands in German. The earliest of these before fol. 65 are dated at end 1501, those following are in later scripts of the first quarter of the 16th century. 

Ff. 2-37 On urines. Fol. 38 Virtus naturalis, virtus animalis, virtus vitalis. Ft. 39-43 De judicio pulsus. Fol. 45 De minutione sanguinis. 46 De medicina, de medicinis. Ff.56v-65 Regimen, etc. with some receipts: Latin and German: the last (fol. 65v) dated in red 1501. 66-end Receipts by various hands, in German.</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">German</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_539_1">
